  Let $h(x) = x abs(x)$. What is $h' (0)$?

  + It is 0.
  + It doesn't exist because $abs(x)$ is not
    differentiable at $0$.
  + It doesn't exist because the right- and
    left-limits, when computing the
    derivative, are different.
  + It doesn't exist because it has a corner.
  + It doesn't exist for a different reason.
